 "remarks": "Some properties are defined as much by what surrounds them as by what can be built.  On New Canaan's prestigious West Side, 230 and 244 West Road comprise two approved building lots totaling 4.91 acres (2.34 and 2.57 acres, respectively), bordering 42 acres of permanently protected land trust. The adjoining conservation acreage provides an enduring natural backdrop within an established landscape of significant estates, just minutes from the village.  Offered together, the parcels present the possibility of creating an estate of considerable scale and distinction. Individually, each offers an exceptional setting for a custom residence.  Conceptual architectural renderings illustrate one potential approach, featuring a residence of approximately 6,000 to 8,000+ square feet. Buyers may explore these concepts or pursue an entirely individual architectural direction.  An offering distinguished by its setting, flexibility, and the freedom to define what comes next.  List price reflects land only; home construction is not included.",
